           So the number carries the precision and the star is a single glanceable
           cue — which is also exactly how the source presents it: Google's own
           place card reads "4.8 ★ (20)". `Stars` (ReviewGrid.tsx) still draws the
           five-glyph row on the review CARDS, where a per-review rating is a
           whole number and the row is therefore exact. -->
      <div class="u-surface-depth mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 rounded-card border border-line/40 bg-surface px-5 py-4">
        {
          /* THE AGGREGATE'S HONESTY VALVE. `rating`/`count` are nullable on
             purpose (see testimonials.ts): if the listing is ever re-read and the
             numbers cannot be confirmed, they go back to `null` and the strip must
             STOP printing them rather than keep showing a claim nobody checked.
